  "helpAutoArchive": {
    "message": "Like Arc, tabs you haven't looked at for a while are closed and kept in the Archive (the box button in Today), where you can reopen them. Chrome's pinned tabs, the dedicated tabs of Favorites, Pinned tabs and GitHub pull requests, the current tab, tabs playing audio and tabs in Incognito windows are never archived. A tab with unsaved input shows Chrome's leave-page prompt and is left open if you cancel."
